] [17592186508880 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508738 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508880 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508880 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508880 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508880 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c1172f21-48d5-50a2-8bbb-2e078be6a776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186508766 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186508636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508903 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f4450d37-cda0-50d9-ad71-0e2c1df13152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508933 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508933 #edb/ref 1069 "q-62054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508933 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508933 #edb/ref 1071 "The daily milk production on Debbie's farm has decreased at a rate of $12%$ every month. If the daily milk production was $1\\,130$ liters initially, then which function correctly represents $p(t),$ the daily milk production after $t$ months?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508933 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5be49d8c-c7c0-5d12-b018-ff8157121a39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508933 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\np(t)=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=1\\,130$ is the initial daily milk production.\n\n- $r=0.12$ is the decay rate ($12%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in months.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $p$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=1\\,130\\cdot (1-0.12)^{t}=1\\,130\\cdot (0.88)^{t}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508944 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508853 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508944 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61793" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508944 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508944 #edb/ref 1071 "The population of a certain animal species is declining at a rate of $3%$ per year. If the species' initial population was $5\\,000$ when the observations started, then which function correctly represents $y(t),$ the population of the species after $t$ years?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508944 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "76eb003d-42ac-559c-8f1c-f5ce54d3972f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508944 #edb/ref 1074 "The formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay rate $r$) is\n\n$$\ny(t)=a(1-r)^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=5\\,000$ is the initial population.\n\n- $r=0.03$ is the decay rate ($3%$ expressed as a decimal).\n\n- $t=$ the time, in years.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=5\\,000\\cdot (1-0.03)^{t}=5\\,000\\cdot (0.97)^{t}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508949 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508863 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508949 #edb/ref 1069 "q-61704" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508949 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508949 #edb/ref 1071 "Ralf is investigating the effect of a substance on some bacteria. In the beginning, there were $3\\,000$ bacteria. After introducing the substance, Ralf noticed that the number of bacteria reduces by $\\frac{1}{4}$ every minute.\n\nThe function $y(t)$ models the number of bacteria after $t$ minutes and is given by\n\n$$\ny(t)=3\\,000\\cdot {(\\text{___})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat number is missing?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "87d542d6-aac4-513b-9fc9-107312f9fcdf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508949 #edb/ref 1074 "If the number of alive bacteria reduces by $\\frac{1}{4}$ every minute, then $\\frac{3}{4}$ of the bacteria remains every minute. So the decay factor is $\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay factor $b$) is\n\n$$\ny=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=3\\,000$ is the initial number of bacteria.\n\n- $b=\\frac{3}{4}$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t=$ the time, in minutes.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $y(t)$ is\n\n$$\ny(t)=3\\,000\\cdot {(\\frac{3}{4})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo the missing number is $\\frac{3}{4}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508994 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186508903 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508994 #edb/ref 1069 "q-62062" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508994 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508994 #edb/ref 1071 "Joel invested $$11\\,280.$ The investment performed poorly, losing one-eighth of its value every month.\n\nThe function $p(t)$ models the value of the investment after $t$ months and is given by\n\n$$\np(t)=11\\,280\\cdot {(\\text{___})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nWhat number is missing?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508994 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec5e8c7c-c10d-59da-bddc-7ee7a7739de6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186508994 #edb/ref 1074 "The initial investment was $$11\\,280$, and this decreased by $\\frac{1}{8}$ every month.\n\nIf the investment value is reduced by $\\frac{1}{8},$ then $\\frac{7}{8}$ of its value remained every month. So the decay factor is $\\frac{7}{8}.$\n\nThe formula for exponential decay (in terms of a decay factor $b$) is\n\n$$\np=a{b}^{t}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n- $a=11\\,280$ is the initial investment.\n\n- $b=\\frac{7}{8}$ is the decay factor.\n\n- $t=$ the time, in months.\n\nTherefore, the correct expression for $p(t)$ is\n\n$$\np(t)=11\\,280\\cdot {(\\frac{7}{8})}^{t}.\n$$\n\nSo the missing number is $\\frac{7}{8}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
